   "id": "action-potential",
   "title": "Nerve conduction and sodium-channel block",
   "kind": "Simulation",
   "sub": "The Hodgkin–Huxley model: find the threshold and refractory period, then block the voltage-gated sodium channels, the target of every dental local anaesthetic, and watch the action potential fail.",
   "note": "SciGradify Biology's simulation of one patch of squid axon membrane (the published 1952 equations); tetrodotoxin stands in for a local anaesthetic, which blocks the same channels from inside the axon and depends on pH and nerve-fibre size. It says nothing about doses.",
